From 05e9cfcdf43c0dfe078ed3feb8af4c8bd701fd74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CamiTune contributors
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] CoreAudio: accept persistent device UIDs

Core Audio display names are mutable and are not guaranteed to be unique.
Resolve the existing device configuration value as a persistent UID first,
while retaining display-name lookup for backwards compatibility. Return UID
and display-name pairs from device discovery as expected by the websocket API.
---
 backend_coreaudio.md            |  9 ++++---
 src/coreaudio_backend/device.rs | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/backend_coreaudio.md b/backend_coreaudio.md
index 448cb80..de1ef8f 100644
--- a/backend_coreaudio.md
+++ b/backend_coreaudio.md
@@ -83,9 +83,12 @@ This example configuration will be used to explain the various options specific
 ```
 The parameters marked (*) are optional.
 
-### Device names
-The device names that are used for `device` for both playback and capture are entered
-as shown in the "Audio MIDI Setup" that can be found under "Other" in Launchpad.
+### Device identifiers
+The `device` value for playback and capture can be either a persistent Core Audio UID
+or the device name shown in "Audio MIDI Setup" under "Other" in Launchpad. UIDs are
+recommended because names are not guaranteed to be unique and can be changed by the user.
+Name lookup remains supported for existing configurations.
+
 The name for the 2-channel interface of Soundflower is "Soundflower (2ch)",
 and the built in audio in a MacBook Pro is called "Built-in Output".
 
diff --git a/src/coreaudio_backend/device.rs b/src/coreaudio_backend/device.rs
